To capture audio output programmatically on Android, you must use the AudioRecord API with an AudioPlaybackCaptureConfiguration. This feature requires Android 10 (API level 29) or higher and user consent via a MediaProjection service. 

Directly capturing another app's audio output is a privacy-sensitive operation, and standard apps can only capture audio produced by themselves or with explicit user permission via the screen capture dialog. 

